From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Mar 2026 16:27:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/57] panvk: Add linked shader cache

Device-level hash tables caching FS prologs, compiled once per prolog
key, and the SPD descriptors that link a prolog to a main shader. The
linked entries are keyed on main shader binary pointer identity and FS
prolog parameters.

Invalidate cache entries when a shader is destroyed to prevent stale
pointer matches from malloc address reuse. Device destruction tears
the cache down after panvk_meta_cleanup() so the meta shaders can
still invalidate their entries.

Modeled after src/asahi/vulkan/hk_shader.c's per-shader fast-link cache,
but kept device-level (with an explicit invalidate hook) so a prolog
and its per-main-FS SPD can be reused across pipelines that bind the
same main FS.

Signed-off-by: Christian Gmeiner <cgmeiner@igalia.com>
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/40343>
